  "articleBody": "Installing new bathroom fixtures sounds straightforward, but there are definitely a few things you'll want to think about to make sure everything goes smoothly and stays leak-free. First off, compatibility is huge. Will your desired toilet, basin, shower system, or taps work with your existing plumbing setup and water pressure? Sometimes, you might need to move or upgrade supply and waste lines, which can impact both cost and timing. You also need to consider how your fixtures will integrate with your waterproofing. For example, ensuring watertight connections around tubs, showers, and tap penetrations is critical to prevent water from seeping into walls and floors. It’s not just about the fixture itself; it’s about how it interacts with the entire bathroom system. Think about coordination with tiling too – things like the height of valves, the type and position of drains, and where niches will go. Getting these details right during planning avoids awkward situations and potential rework later on. And don't forget about long-term maintenance; what will be required for seals and caulk to keep everything watertight? Getting these questions answered upfront, possibly with a professional, helps ensure your new fixtures aren't just beautiful, but also functional and durable.",
